        "label": "Launch — Atlas-Agena D",
        "description": "Cape Canaveral, 1964-11-28. The first successful Mars mission of any kind — earlier Soviet attempts (Mars 1960A/B/C) and NASA's Mariner 3 (failed shroud separation 3 weeks before) all collapsed before reaching Mars."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 0.005,
